                            <div class="stat-value" style="color: var(--bar-color-alt);">~13%</div>
                            <div class="stat-label"><strong>United States</strong><br>Declining</div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="stat-card">
                            <div class="stat-value">~8%</div>
                            <div class="stat-label"><strong>India</strong><br>Rising</div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="stat-card">
                            <div class="stat-value" style="color: var(--bar-color-low);">~6%</div>
                            <div class="stat-label"><strong>European Union (27)</strong><br>Declining</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="split-media reveal">
                    <img src="assets/figure_6.jpg" alt="Share of global CO2 emissions by country">
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Slide 5: Per Capita Inequality -->
    <section class="slide">
        <div class="slide-content">
            <div class="slide-header reveal">
                <div class="slide-number">04</div>
                <h2>Per Capita Emissions Range from 0.1 t in Chad to ~14 t in the US and Canada</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="split-layout">
                <div class="split-text reveal">
                    <p>Per capita CO₂ emissions reveal stark global inequalities. The gap is enormous: the average American or Australian emits in under two days what the average person in Mali or Niger emits in an entire year.</p>
                    <ul class="bullet-list">
                        <li><strong>Highest Emitters:</strong> Major oil-producing nations with small populations (e.g., Qatar, UAE).</li>
                        <li><strong>Wealthy Populous Nations:</strong> The US, Australia, and Canada have per capita emissions roughly 3x the global average.</li>
                        <li><strong>150x Difference:</strong> Between the lowest (Sub-Saharan Africa) and highest large-country emitters.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="split-media reveal" style="flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; justify-content: center;">
                    <div class="bar-chart">
                        <div class="bar-row">
                            <div class="bar-label">US / Canada</div>
                            <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill alt" style="width: 100%;">~14 t</div></div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="bar-row">
                            <div class="bar-label">EU (27)</div>
                            <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width: 43%;">~6 t</div></div>
