                <h2>2024 Snapshot: Many Western Nations Cut Emissions While Parts of Asia and Africa Grew</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="split-layout">
                <div class="split-text reveal">
                    <p>The map of annual percentage change in CO₂ emissions for 2024 shows a highly mixed global picture.</p>
                    <ul class="bullet-list">
                        <li><strong>Declines:</strong> Many Western nations—including the US, much of the EU, and the UK—saw emissions drop.</li>
                        <li><strong>Increases:</strong> Russia, parts of Southeast Asia, and several African nations experienced growth.</li>
                        <li><strong>Notable Spikes:</strong> Some countries in Central Asia (e.g., Turkmenistan, Uzbekistan) saw large increases exceeding 10%.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="split-media reveal">
                    <img src="assets/figure_5.jpg" alt="Annual percentage change in CO2 emissions, 2024">
